{title: I know I’m saved}
{subtitle: Hymnal 62}
{x_theme: joy, praise, salvation, heaven}
{x_source: docx:1. Incomplete/I know I_m saved.docx}

{comment: Chorus}
I know I’m saved and I’m so glad about it
I’ve found the joy my spirit craved
It is so real that I could never doubt it
Praise the Lord for I know I’m saved

{comment: Verse 1}
I feel no condemnation upon my soul today
No more am I by sin enslaved
I’m walking now with Jesus along the narrow way
So happy for I know I’m saved

{comment: Verse 2}
My soul is filled with glory I care not any more
For pleasures of this world depraved
I’m satisfied with Jesus, my cup is running o’er
How wonderful to know I’m saved

{comment: Verse 3}
I’m going to a city, the New Jerusalem
When all the storms of life I’ve braved
There I shall see my Savior and ever be with Him
Rejoicing just to know I’m saved
